# Files NOT copied into the Docker build context.
#
# Why this matters: every `COPY` in your Dockerfile starts from a snapshot
# of your repo. Without .dockerignore, Docker uploads your entire repo
# (including node_modules, build artifacts, learning notes, .git) to the
# Docker daemon before the build can start. That's:
#   - slow (every change re-uploads the whole tree)
#   - leaky (your local .env / secrets could be baked into a layer)
#   - bloat-prone (final image ends up containing things you didn't want)
#
# Rule of thumb: ignore anything that doesn't need to compile into the
# binary. Then `git status` and `docker build` see the same surface.

# --- VCS / metadata ---------------------------------------------------------
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github/
.editorconfig

# --- Build artifacts --------------------------------------------------------
bin/
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
*.test
*.out
coverage.*

# --- Local-only / personal --------------------------------------------------
learning-notes/
.env
.env.local
.vscode/
.idea/
.devcontainer/

# --- Tooling configs that don't affect the binary ---------------------------
.dockerignore
Dockerfile
docker-compose*.yml
justfile
Makefile
.pre-commit-config.yaml
.golangci.yml

# --- Docs (markdown is fine inside the image if you want; we exclude here) --
*.md
LICENSE
decisions/

# --- OS junk ----------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# --- Logs -------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
logs/
